<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zanj Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/869">869</a>–883</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Zanj Revolt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanj">Zanj</a> Rebellion was a major revolt in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> from 869 to 883, led by Ali ibn Muhammad and involving enslaved East Africans, known as the Zanj, who laboured in the salt marshes near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a>. The rebels established a state, sacked Basra and defeated Abbasid armies for years before being crushed. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> treat it as a costly crisis that drained resources during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>'s decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zanj-rebellion.jpg" alt="Zanj Rebellion" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ro4444 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zanj_Rebellion.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
